<title>USA: Heska IPO target price is lowered again.</title>
<headline>Heska IPO target price is lowered again.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The proposed target price for the initial public offering in Heska Corp was lowered for the second time, to $8.50 from $10, lead underwriter Credit Suisse First Boston said Friday.</p>
<p>Previously, the estimated price range of $14 to $16 was cut to a target of $10.</p>
<p>The offering comprises 5.35 million shares under the symbol &quot;HSKA&quot; on the Nasdaq National Market.</p>
<p>Heska, which manufactures animal health products, is expected to trade next Tuesday.</p>
